0 i.e. lover of husbandry (or do these point to earlier meaning tillage ? compare Dl Pr 105 ) א עֹבֵד ׳אִישׁ Zech 13:5 . 2 piece of ground , landed property Gen 47:18-19 , (3 t. in verse); 47:20 , 22 (twice in verse); 47:23 , 26 (all J) Psa 49:12 (plural) 3 earth as material substance; of which man is made Gen 2:7 ( מִןהָֿא ׳עָפָד ); so animals 2:19 ( ׳מִןהָֿא ); altar Exod 20:24 ; earthen vessels א ׳חַרְשֵׂי Isa 45:9 ; on head, sign of woe 1Sam 4:12 ; 2Sam 1:2 ; 15:32 ; of contrition Neh 9:1 (compare עָפָר אֵפֶר, ; הָא ׳מַעֲבֵה 1Kin 7:46 compare 2Chr 4:17 ( firmness of earth , firm earth, clay-ground, for casting-moulds; or clay-moulds (Berthau) ? or is this n.pr. ? Klo proposes הָאֲדֻמָּה בַּמְּעָרָה in the red cave ); mule-loads of 2Kin 5:17 ; in it lie the dead אַדְמַתעָֿפָר מִיְּשֵׁנֵי Dan 12:2 compare Gen 3:19 , 23 ; Psa 146:4 . 4 ground as earth's visible surface; הָא ׳רֶמֶס Gen 1:25 ; 6:20 (both P) Hosea 2:20 compare Gen 7:8 ; 9:2 (J ?) Lev 20:25 (P) Deut 4:18 ; Ezek 38:20 ; also Gen 4:10 (J) Isa 24:21 ; Amos 3:5 ; Zeph 1:2-3 , as wet with dew 2Sam 17:12 ; rain 1Kin 17:14 ; 18:1 ; compare personified הָא ׳מָּֽצְתָה אֶתמִּֿיהָ Num 16:30 (P) (|| ארץ 16:32 ), see 16:31 ; of particular place, spot ׳א קֹדֶשׁ Exod 3:5 especially as abode of man Gen 4:11 ; Exod 10:6 ; Deut 4:10 , 40 ; 12:1 ; 1Sam 20:31 ; 2Sam 14:7 ; often הָא ׳מְּנֵי Gen 2:6 ; 4:14 ; 6:1 , 7 ; 7:4 , 23 ; 8:8 , 13 ; Exod 32:12 ; 33:16 ; Num 12:3 ; Deut 6:15 ; 7:6 (all J, D) 1Sam 20:15 9 t. 5 land, territory, country (= ארץ ) Gen 47:19 (J) Lev 20:24 (J ? — || ארץ ) construct before proper name ׳א מִצְרַיִם Gen 47:20 , 26 ; ׳א יְהוּדָה Isa 19:17 ; ׳א יִשְׂרָאֵל Ezek 11:17 16 t. Ezekiel; especially of land as promised or given by ׳י to his people = Canaan Gen 28:15 ; Exod 20:12 ; Num 11:12 ; 32:11 (all J ?) Deut 5:16 16 t. Deuteronomy, Joshua; 1Kin 8:34 , 40 +; Jer 16:15 ; 24:10 ; 25:5 ; 35:15 ; Ezek 28:25 ; 2Chr 6:25 , 31 ; 7:20 ; 33:8 ; compare also Deut 12:19 ; 21:23 ; 29:27 ; 2Kin 17:23 ; Isa 6:11 ; 7:1